    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="1033" n="1005" xml:id="pg1005"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/5–2154: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aldrich</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d698-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-05-21T11:00:00+01:00">May 21, 1954—11
                            a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5253. Re Austrian UN membership Foreign Office concurs with Department’s position
                    (Deptel 5721, April 28).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d698-f2"/> Delay in reaching
                    decision due to second thoughts on Austria’s eligibility for membership in view
                    of its occupation status. Legal staff which in 1949 found Austria eligible has
                    now reversed itself. Hence Foreign Office considers any action beyond Austrian
                    letter to UN SYG undesirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldrich</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
